<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) (Confuciusornis sanctus)",
        "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Confuciusornis sanctus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3152_confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Confuciusornis sanctus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3152_confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Confuciusornis sanctus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That melanosome length equals 143.4 µm",
        "does_not_claim: That the Senckenberg slab outline is a Turing pattern",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.08, b=1.12, Du=0.5, Dv=6.0 chosen so λ_c = 143.4 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral split-step on a periodic 8-wavelength collar",
        "reported_in_source: Barb-ridge spacing is an activator-inhibitor process (Harris et al. 2005)",
        "reported_in_source: Confuciusornis sanctus is a beaked pygostylian with ribbon rectrices and preserved feather pigment",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion relation",
        "reported_in_source: Within-feather pigment bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion pattern (Prum & Williamson 2002)",
        "transfer_boundary: 143.4 µm is the slot scale, not a new measurement of a fossil barb",
        "transfer_boundary: The numerical kinetics are a carrier of k_c, not a parameter table from the feather papers" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Confuciusornis sanctus (Early Cretaceous (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Confuciusornis" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3152_confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Confuciusornis sanctus; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion relation | Within-feather pigment bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion pattern (Prum & Williamson 2002) | Barb-ridge spacing is an activator-inhibitor process (Harris et al. 2005) | Confuciusornis sanctus is a beaked pygostylian with ribbon rectrices and preserved feather pigment; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.08, b=1.12, Du=0.5, Dv=6.0 chosen so λ_c = 143.4 µm | Spectral split-step on a periodic 8-wavelength collar; transfer_boundary: The numerical kinetics are a carrier of k_c, not a parameter table from the feather papers | 143.4 µm is the slot scale, not a new measurement of a fossil barb; does_not_claim: That the Senckenberg slab outline is a Turing pattern | That melanosome length equals 143.4 µm]; phenomenon_size: 109 µm (0.0001086 m, log10=-3.964 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 109 µm to 24.4 cm): 109 µm:confuciusornis-sanctus-bioelectric-polarity, 340 µm:confuciusornis-sanctus-vertex-packing, 5.4 mm:confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength, 1.1 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-clock-wavefront, 2.4 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-morphogen-condensation, 3.0 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-elastic-buckling, 3.4 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-flux-canalization, 4.8 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-branching-tree" ;
